      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>HAVE YOU TRIED</head>
        <p>HAVE YOU TRIED</p>
        <p>WHITE eeft</p>
        <p>SELF.RAIS"NG FLOUR?</p>
        <p>IF NOT, WHY OT?N</p>
        <p>Wholesale by</p>
        <p>J. POVEY &amp; SON, Ltd.,</p>
        <p>BRIDGE STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Church Notices.</p>
        <p>CHRISTADELPHIAN MEETING ROOM, BOLD-STREET. WARRINGTON. Pree Bible Address SUNDAY NEXT, at 6.30 p.m. Subject: "The Christian Citizenship: Its Divine Principles and Claims." By Mr. T. GRIFFITHS. of Birkenhead.</p>
        <p>Public Notices.</p>
        <p>COUNTY, BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that BANK PAR,I. WILL BE CLOSED</p>
        <p>to the General Public ON SATURDAY, THE 3RD OF JUNE, from 2.30 to 6.30 p.m.</p>
        <p>VOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. ‘-) A MEETING will be held at the TOWN HALL on TUESDAY EVENING NEXT, the 23rd inst., at 8 o'clock, for the purpose of NOMINATING A REPRESENTATIVE OF LABOUR upon THE LOCAL NAVAL AND MILITARY WAR PENSIONS COMMITTEE. All Trade Unions are requested to send two Delegates to the Meeting. PETER PEACOCK, Mayor.</p>
        <p>rnuE CORPORATION OF WARRINGTON -IL is prepared to receive LOANS either for SiX months' notice or for a term of years. Applications, stating amount for investment, to be made to the Borough Treasurer, Municipal Office,s, Warrington. COIJNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. ROLL OF HONOUR</p>
        <p>FOR WARRINGTON HEROES. I shall be glad if the relatives and friends of Warrington Soldiers and Sailors who have lcst their lives in the War will be good enough to send to me as soon as possible the full names and addressgs and the names of the Regiment or Ship in which the Soldiers and Sailors served, in order that a complete and an accurate ROLL OF HONOUR to, their Memory may be pre- pared</p>
        <p>PETER PEACOCK, Mayor. Mayor's Parlour, Town Hall, 26th May, 1916.</p>
        <p>• JOSEPH BAMFORTH, LIMITED. VOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, pursuant to 4-1 Section 188 of the Companies (Consolidation) Act, 1908. that a Meeting of the Creditors of Joseph Bamforth, Limited, will be held at 2, Egypt-street, Warrington, in the County of Lancaster, on Monday, the sth day of June, 1916, at ten o'clock in the fore- noon, for the purposes provided for in the said Section. Dated the 22nd day of May, 1916. LOUISA J. BAMPORTH, 'Witness: Josh. Longland, Liquidator. Yolicitor, 2, Egypt-street, Warrington. NORTHERN CIRCUIT SUMMER ASSIZES, 1916.</p>
        <p>LANCASTER. The Commissions 03 r holding these Assizes will he opened at Lancaster on WEDNESDAY, the 14th June. The Court will sit on THURSDAY, the 15th June, at 11 o'clock a.m. LIVERPOOL.</p>
        <p>, The Commissions for Assizes will he opened at Liverpool on MONDAY, the 19th UDR. The Court will sit on TUESDAY, the 20th June, at 11 o'clock a.m. The regulations for conducting the Criminal Business will be published in due time. -MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>, The Commissioni;iaiii-o-lili-n-iihese Assizes will ')e opened at Manchester on MONDAY, the 10th July. „ The Court will sit on TUESDAY, the 11th dulv, at 11 o'clock a.m. ,The regulations for conducting the Criminal lousiness will be published in due time. BAIL CASES will be taken at the above 4188izes.</p>
        <p>HERBERT STEPHEN, Clerk of Assize. Office of Clerk of Assize, Preston. 18th May, 1916. TiN•l3.—lt is particularly requested that all 1-"ePositions, Inquisitions, and Recognisances Iliad be immediately forwarded to me at Preston.</p>
