      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0128" n="art0128">
        <head>AND PUBLIC-HOUSES.</head>
        <p>AND PUBLIC-HOUSES.</p>
        <p>Funeral of Well-known Licensee And Sportsman.</p>
        <p>Ofi Monday a large number of relatives and friends attended the funeral of Mr. T. Nixon, who passed away at his residence, the Black Bear Inn, on Friday of last week. The deceased gentleman, Who was fifty-five years of age, had been in failing health for some time past, and since February had been confined to his room. He was a keen and prominent sportsman, being a leading official of the Warrington Anglers' Association, trea- surer of the Mersey Gun Club, president of the Latchford Garden Society, and treasurer of the Latchford Angling Ststiety. He was also a member of the Wine and Beer Sellers' Associa- tion, and chairman of the Rational Friendly Society( The interment took place at the Grappenhall Parish Church, being preceded by a short ser- vice conducted by the Rev. H. V. Pigot at the home of the deceased. The chief mourners were: Mr. John Nixon and Mr. Joseph Nixon (brothers), Mr. S2Snutch (half-brother), Mr. D. Patterson (son-in-law),</p>
