      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0180" n="art0180">
        <head>SHOOTING.</head>
        <p>SHOOTING.</p>
        <p>importanl Match For Trophy</p>
        <p>At Appieton.</p>
        <p>The Appleton Rifle Range on Saturday after- ndon was the venue of an important shooting competition between the 4th Battalion Manches- ter, Volunteer Regiment, and. the lstlßattalion •(GUard).. Regiment, Liverpool, •in • connection with 'the.- County Palatine of Lancaster Rifle a (Small Bore) Association for • the trophy, a handsome silver bowl, presented by Colonel J. Johnston, V.D., D.L., who is the regimental ir mmandant of the Lanca- shire Volunteer Brigade. There was a large gathering or interested 'spectators. The competition proper took place early in this. month, on • the competing clubs' own ranges, 41 teams entering. ;- The Manchester and Liverpool teams, cane out on top, and Appleton ;Range- was selected, for ,the final, The Men- ehester .team won by 28 points, the .seore,,•.b.ing Manchester 1.160, Liverpool. 1432. The, pf;s sible" was 1,200. _ _ _</p>
        <p>Colonel Johnston, in presenting the trophy to the captain of the winning- team (Mr. A. 11. Parker), and silver spoons, .as a souvenir,• to the six members of each team, expressed the Rime .that' n great Many more .men -.lt-Cglit be induced to take up rifle shooting, not only be- Cause they would be rendering a national Kr- vice by doing so, but because it would be a pleasure to them. A nation of marksmen would tend to bring to a speedier conclusion the terrible struggle in Which we were now engaged.' Every marksman should realise fully the great responsibility that was placed on his.shouldars in utilising the knowledge he had gained at the hands of the musketry instructor. (Hear. hear.) The company later met at- the Lion Hotel, Warrington, , and had tea. Congratulatory speeches :were delivered, and the evening spent in harmony.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0181" n="art0181">
