      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0182" n="art0182">
        <head>LAST OF THE GRACES.</head>
        <p>THE LAST OF THE GRACES.</p>
        <p>Dr. Alfred .Grace, elder brother of the late pr. W. G Grace, died at his 'home at Chipping Sodbury, near Bristol, on Wednesday aged 76. He was the last survivor of the notable family of. crieketers,"*and was himself a good player, though never so prominent as his three brothers. He had been fifty years in medical practice at Chipping Sedbury.</p>
        <p>MEMBER' FOR WIDNES.</p>
        <p>Unopposed Re-election Of Colonel Hall Walker.</p>
        <p>Nominations for the , Parliamentary vacancy in the Widnes Division closed on Monday. Colonel Hall Walker (Conservative), who had held the seat for sixteen .yeaA, was returned unopposed. He had the -support of Conserva- tives and Liberals. The by-election wag' neces- sitated by Colonel Hall Walker's retirement on his gift to the Government of his .racing studs .at Tulley and Riissley -Park, valued - at .V 75,000 and the sale ,on the Government's own valua- tion of both estates. • •</p>
      </div>
