        <p>THE 222nd QUARTERLY MEETING of the Warrington EL Co-oporative Societu Ltd. lw held in the CO-OPERATIVE HALL, CAIRO STREET, on Monday Evening Next, May 29th, at 8 o'clock. Admission to Members only on production. of Membership Ticket. . Business Important. A goOd attendance requested. Subject to the Quarterly Meeting's approval, Dividend will .be paid on all purchases made during the Quarter ended 'April 18th at the rate of 3/- in the X. This means over £17,000 being returned to Members, saved to them by the Society in three months. The annual average Saving (returned in dividend) during the past four years exceeds £4 per member per annum. Prices are reasonable. Goods are of the Finest Quality. You can save money easily even in War Time by Joining the Co-opera- tive Society.' Apply at the Office for all particulars. J. JARMAN, Secretary.</p>
        <p>READ THIS! (Copied from the ORIGIN AL by Proprietors of this Paper.) DEAR MR. WOOD, 22nd May, 1916. I have been successful in obtaining a post with a firm in Warrington, to which you recommended me, at a commencing salary of 25/- (twenty-five shillings) per week. This success I attribute to the splendid tuition I received whilst attending your College. Thanking you for your kindness in the past, I remain, Yours sincerely, Full day classes 17i6. Half-day attendance 12/6. Evening classes from 7/6 per month. WOOD'S COLLEGE, 15, Bridge St., Warrington.</p>
